title: 'For Drew: more folders are redrawn at a switch, so point inside any root folder now moves to the root at a switch, not only inside the containers folder.'
pid: 8afc6936-a2b3-4758-9013-1a2a8b59f711
body: |2-
  A redrawn folder hidden in the root stays hidden, but its members are
  drawn anew, unfolded, with new viewnode IDs. Also yours: a root
  write-protected because the fork it was re-pointed to is editable
  deeper in the same view stays write-protected when switched back (the
  last child here). And the
  subscribee as such in a fresh view of a fork is drawn write-protected
  with no unintegrated children, only its count; I noted a guess why
  under "It is drawn only where the subscribee is drawn" in my map, but
  it is drawing, and yours if anyone's.
